\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The \textsc  {ReActive}{} paradigm: \emph  {Re} $+$ \emph  {Act} $+$ \emph  {ively}. ReAct supplies the first two halves---an inner think--act--observe loop; the third half is that the loop is entered by the world, not by an instruction. An experience is recalled before reasoning begins and is revised after acting, so the same situation is not reasoned about twice.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
